        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35897452?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Safari also supports SVG WebExtension icons so the note should be updated to include it.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">The page currently contradicts itself: the note about SVG WebExtension icon support says the feature is only available in Firefox, while the compatibility notes say support was added to Safari a couple of months later.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">The compatibility notes state the feature is available in Safari: <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/manifest.json/icons#browser_compatibility\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/manifest.json/icons#browser_compatibility</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41052",
            "title": "Safari also supports SVG WebExtension icons",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-07T21:55:17.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-07T21:53:02.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "stevennyman",
                "url": "https://github.com/stevennyman"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add a release note describing support for <code class=\"notranslate\">getBytesInUse()</code> supported in <code class=\"notranslate\">local</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">managed</code> storage. Also, updates the Firefox support note on <code class=\"notranslate\">getBytesInUse()</code>. Addresses the dev-docs-needed requirements of <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1385832\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1385832</a> getBytesInUse() is not supported in <code class=\"notranslate\">local</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">managed</code> storage areas</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">BCD updates in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3390676588\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27769\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27769/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27769\">mdn/browser-compat-data#27769</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41046",
            "title": "Bug-1385832 getBytesInUse supported in local and managed release noter",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-06T18:48:06.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-06T18:45:54.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67789862?u=026c90580590cfbc3e63c7a97793ba493fa46fbc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The AbortController <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortController/AbortController#examples\" rel=\"nofollow\">examples</a> include code that reused the same AbortController instance across multiple fetch calls, which causes them to be instantly cancelled.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The documentation should be updated to help developers understand that an AbortController instance cannot be reused.</p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41043",
            "title": "Fix AbortController being reused in multiple fetch requests in some o…",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-10T17:15:27.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-06T14:13:31.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "marcindz88",
